v0.97.6
---

New:
- notORM: support for named fields
- notORM: assoc array back-resolution (fill out an array from named fields)
- notORM: data_add with autoincrement will return last element ID to the caller
          in the variable $notORM_id
- changelog: initial support; searches for breaking changes and notifies the admin after an upgrade
- template: implemented special -unset- type

Fixes:
- notORM: fix an off-by-one causing some queries to return empty

Misc:
- attempted to improve the FreeBSD compat situation, with limited success
- fixed scope on some variables in misc
- initial probe read can now timeout, should reduce hung processes

BREAKING:
- removed support for ncat due to numerous bugs
- removed support for listening with TLS due to ncat dependency

v0.97.5
---

New:
- migrations (run-once scripts for clean upgrades; see docs/migrations.md)
- util/account.sh (helper for managing accounts from console)

Fixed:
- server: parsing fixes
- http_array shows a single value if the request didn't contain a real array


v0.97.4
---

New:
- API for accessing HTTP arrays (`http_array`)

Misc:
- unified internal API for parsing urlencoded GET/POST params
- perf: reduced amount of basename calls in vhost logic
- docs improvements


v0.97.3.1
---

Fixes:
- `${r[@]}` is no logner mangled by data_iter
- remove spurious git invocation in backticks in the upgrade reminder code


v0.97.3
---

New:
- helper utils (maintenance scripts running in a known environment, invoked with
  `./http.sh <utilname>`. list of utils: `./http.sh utils`)
- util/bump: new util
- util/notORM: new util

Fixes:
- socat now properly binds without IPv6 routes
- template: better handling of nonexistant files
- allow httpsh to be invoked with a PWD that's not the root dir


v0.97.2
---

Description: bugfix release.

Fixed:
- template: fix a hypothetical LFI in the include paths
- template: default include path now processed properly


v0.97.1
---

Description: (this is an old release, changes are handpicked. look at git log for more details)

BREAKING:
- template paths are now relative to the namespace directory (usually `app/`). Check the docs,
  or set `template_relative_paths="./"` to bring back the previous behavior.

New:
- notORM: support new syntax for data_yeet and data_iter
- websocket: full rewrite, new APIs
- server: generic r[url_clean]

Fixed:
- notORM: fix a couple regressions
- secfixes: fix a template bug that could be chained to RCE

Misc:
- relicense to BSD-3-Clause

